I tried to send you a mail - but maybe it did not get through... Most 
probably you have a file protection problem. The playground directory 
must be world-writable (nethack will try to create files in it). Also 
remember, that if the playground is not a top-level directory all its 
parents must be at least world-readable.  Also files: logfile, perm
and record in the playground must be world-writeable. I have various 
versions of nethack instaled on several VMS machines without such
problems...
